&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like SBI, Money Forward, Paradigm, Dragonfly, Galaxy, and PayPal Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will support accounts payable and receivables for Mesh on a part-time basis, using Bill.com, NetSuite and AI-assisted invoice processing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage the AP inbox and review bills captured in Bill.com before they route for approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect vendor forms (W-9, W-8BEN) and file new-contractor reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer routine vendor questions and follow up on missing card receipts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Send scheduled payment reminders and first collection follow-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clear older and miscoded bills in the first two months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of accounts payable or receivable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bill.com and NetSuite experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable availability during US business hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent written English; Spanish a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like SBI, Money Forward, Paradigm, Dragonfly, Galaxy, and PayPal Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh is building the financial operating system that connects exchanges, wallets, and payment flows across the digital asset ecosystem. As we scale, we&#39;re looking for a Chief of Staff to be the CEO&#39;s closest strategic partner and the executive who makes the company run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to our Founder and CEO, you&#39;ll own how Mesh operates. You&#39;ll set the operating rhythm, drive the company&#39;s highest-priority initiatives, and oversee the Business Operations function. You&#39;ll extend the CEO&#39;s reach across the company, turning strategy into plans, plans into accountable owners, and owners into results. This is an executive seat on the leadership team: you&#39;ll own outcomes, not just coordinate them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the CEO&#39;s strategic thinking partner on company priorities, key decisions, and tradeoffs, and represent the CEO with the exec team, board, partners, and investors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Mesh&#39;s operating rhythm: annual and quarterly planning, OKRs, weekly leadership reviews, exec meetings, and town halls, so priorities are clear, progress is visible, and decisions don&#39;t stall&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead board and investor readiness, including quarterly board updates, exec summaries, and company performance reporting built on a single source of truth for key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the Business Operations function, partnering with the Biz Ops lead to set priorities, remove blockers, and raise the bar for how cross-functional work is scoped, run, and measured&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive CEO special projects end to end, from new markets and strategic partnerships (exchanges, wallets, on/off-ramp partners) to pricing and unit economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the executive team accountable to company goals, surface risks early, and resolve the cross-functional issues that sit between teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People on org design, executive hiring, internal communications, and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the systems, dashboards, and AI-powered workflows that make company performance easy to see and let Mesh scale efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience, including senior leadership in strategy and operations, business operations, or as a Chief of Staff to a CEO at a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven people leader who has managed teams and overseen multiple functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has owned (not just supported) a company operating cadence: planning, OKRs, exec reviews, and board preparation at a scaling startup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and sound judgment; trusted by the CEO, board, and exec team, and comfortable giving direct feedback upward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communicator who can turn complexity into clear narratives for the board, leadership, and the whole company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven and commercially minded; comfortable building models and owning company metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in crypto and/or payments processing (stablecoins, exchanges, wallets, on/off-ramps, card and payment networks, regulatory licensing), with a network across the ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth startup environments (Series B and beyond preferred) and able to travel, including internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to be in the office 3 days a week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. For candidates outside of New York or San Francisco, compensation will be adjusted to reflect the applicable market and location-based pay band. The base salary range listed excludes commission (if applicable), equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$250,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$275,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, you&#39;re not stepping into a typical role—you&#39;re joining a rocket ship in mid-liftoff. You&#39;ll tackle complex, meaningful problems that actually move an industry forward, working alongside a sharp, motivated team that moves quickly, collaborates deeply, and expects everyone to operate with ownership. This is the kind of place where you&#39;ll see your work ship fast, make real impact, and be able to point to something and say, &quot;I built that.&quot; You&#39;ll grow fast, level up your skills, and get a front-row seat to how a high-growth company scales from the inside, with competitive comp, solid benefits, and room to stretch your craft all coming standard. If you&#39;re energized by building, learning, and shaping something big—this is where you&#39;ll want to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Office Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees based in our &lt;strong&gt;San Francisco, New York, and Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; hubs are expected to work from the office at least 40% of the time (approximately two days per week). This expectation may vary slightly depending on role, team, and business needs. Certain roles that require closer cross-functional collaboration or operational support may have additional in-office requirements, which will be discussed during the interview process. Our hybrid approach is designed to balance meaningful in-person collaboration, team building, and real-time decision-making with the flexibility to work remotely. We believe this structure supports strong execution while preserving autonomy and focus time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Care For Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great work happens when people feel valued and supported. That starts with competitive salary and equity that grows as you and the company grow, plus comprehensive health coverage for you and your family. We offer unlimited PTO—and we mean it. Take the time you need to recharge and show up at your best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re invested in your growth with a dedicated budget for courses, conferences, and certifications. Work from wherever you&#39;re most productive with our remote-friendly approach, and count on having the top-tier tools and equipment you need to do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh Pay is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, genetic information, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, lawful alien status, national origin, age, marital status, and non-job related physical or mental disability, or protected veteran status. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Mesh, our mission is to enable consumers to pay and be paid with any asset. Today, trillions of dollars in tokenized assets exist but remain largely unusable for everyday commerce. Mesh is bridging this gap by making crypto payments reliable, useful, and ubiquitous. We combine a powerful orchestration engine with a seamless consumer app to unlock liquidity for the world. Backed by leading investors like SBI, Money Forward, Paradigm, Dragonfly, Galaxy, and PayPal Ventures, we are building the infrastructure for the next era of the global economy. Join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mesh is hiring its first dedicated Compliance Officer for its Japan entity. This is a foundational role. You will not inherit a function; you will build one: policies, procedures, and controls designed for a crypto payments infrastructure business operating under Japanese regulation. You will work closely with outside counsel and Mesh’s global compliance team, and you will be the person regulators, partners, and internal stakeholders come to first on anything compliance-related in Japan. The role can start as full-time or as a fractional engagement, depending on the right person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and maintain Mesh Japan’s compliance program, including AML/CFT, KYC and Travel Rule obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for regulatory engagement and licensing-related workstreams in Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with outside counsel on regulatory filings and ongoing obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build policies and procedures fit for a crypto payments infrastructure business operating in Japan, not adapted from a generic template.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track regulatory developments in Japan’s digital-asset and payments space and advise leadership on what they mean for Mesh.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Mesh’s global compliance, legal and risk teams to keep Japan practices aligned with company-wide standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding and due diligence for new partners and clients in Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare compliance reporting for the board and for regulators as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in compliance, regulatory affairs or legal roles within financial services, payments, or crypto and digital assets in Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of Japan’s regulatory framework for payments and/or crypto-asset businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or reporting to the FSA or a comparable regulator, directly or through counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial license applications with Regional Finance Bureaus (RFB) and the FSA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level fluency in Japanese and English; native Japanese speaker preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort building a function from the ground up with limited initial resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and strong written communication for policy and regulatory documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The estimated base salary for this position is¥15,00,000 to ¥30,000,000. The compensation range provided may span multiple career levels and will be narrowed during the interview process based on factors including a candidate&#39;s experience, skills, qualifications, and geographic location. The base salary range listed excludes commission (if applicable), equity, and benefits. The pay range represents the minimum and maximum target for new-hire compensation. Actual compensation may vary and may be higher or lower depending on individual circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love It Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
